Map meson's 'sunos' to 'solaris' in the compiled-in Nix system string.

On illumos and Solaris, meson's host_machine.system() is 'sunos', so Nix reports
x86_64-sunos. nixpkgs has no 'sunos' kernel: its double is x86_64-solaris, and
lib.systems fails with "Unknown kernel: sunos". Report the name nixpkgs uses.

--- a/src/libstore/meson.build
+++ b/src/libstore/meson.build
@@ -53,3 +53,3 @@
   'NIX_LOCAL_SYSTEM',
-  nix_system_cpu + '-' + host_machine.system(),
+  nix_system_cpu + '-' + (host_machine.system() == 'sunos' ? 'solaris' : host_machine.system()),
   description : 'This is the system name Nix expects for local running instance of Nix.\n\n'
